// The OpenAPI contract's request half (#719). Scoped by biome.jsonc to packages/*/src/**.
//
// A route declares what it accepts with `validate(target, Schema)` from
// `@pithy-sh/core/src/http/validation`. That is `zValidator` with the one failure hook applied and the
// schema left readable on the middleware, which is how the contract finds it in a composed app. A bare
// `zValidator(...)` still validates, so nothing at runtime notices; the schema just never reaches the
// document, and every client generated from it is missing that part of the request. So it is refused
// here, the one place it can be. `validation.ts` is the single call site that may name it.
language js

`zValidator($...)` as $call where {
  register_diagnostic(span=$call, message="A bare zValidator hides its schema from the OpenAPI contract. Use validate(target, Schema) from @pithy-sh/core/src/http/validation.")
}
